A||||8||Dan87GT||Subwoofer Replacement Speaker||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||03-28-2000||07:32 AM||||Anybody know of a good replacement speaker for the factory sub system?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||03-28-2000||10:01 AM||||The factory sub takes a 5.25" speaker, right?  Crutchfield sells Polk and Rockford Fosgate 5.25" speakers that look pretty nice - they're listed as "midrange" but I think it'll be nearly impossible to find a speaker that small listed as a woofer.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-8Ireu3XKVXY/ProdGroup.asp?grp=440&sid=S-8Ireu3XKVXY&store=0" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-8Ireu3XKVXY/ProdGroup.asp?grp=440&sid=S-8Ireu3XKVXY&store=0</A> <P>I'm sure these speakers are better than the factory GM.  Only problem is, I think you can only get these in pairs.  Maybe another Fieroholic with Performance Sound would split a pair with you?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-28-2000||10:16 AM||||Radio Shack Sells a "long throw" 5.25 woofer.<BR>The woofer is designed for extended bass. It's 8 ohms. Stock GM is 10 ohms and car 5.25 speakers are 4 ohms. The lower the ohms the more distortion you will get out of the GM amp.||||reg||4
Z||000003||Formula||03-28-2000||10:48 AM||||I just happen to have a JL audio 5.25" midrange that has a small (very small) rip in the surround that I dont want or need.<P>E-mail me if you want it.  (pay for shipping and its yours)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan87GT||03-28-2000||11:39 AM||||Can I put a resistor in the line to make up the difference?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||03-28-2000||12:16 PM||||If you go with the Radio Shack speaker you don't really need the resistor. It will sound louder but just don't crank it all the way up. If your using a car speaker I would suggest getting a resistor otherwise you'll drive the amp too hard and it could overheat and fail. I have replaced factory subs with the radio shack speaker and have had no problems. Using a car speaker sometimes you have to add foam to the inside of the sub enclosure because the enclosure is too large for the midrange 5.25 speaker. (Also you can buy the radio shack speaker as 1 they don't sell them as pairs)||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||03-28-2000||02:42 PM||||I thought the factory (woofer) speaker was 4 ohms. At least that is what the one that was in mine was and it looked too bad (surround rotted) to not be factory.<P>BTW, Rodney is showing a factory replacement as "coming soon". rodney???<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 03-28-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000007||AL||03-28-2000||10:11 PM||||i agree radio shack sounds, ||||reg||14
Z||000008||Rodney||03-28-2000||10:47 PM||||Have a speaker that I have done some R&D on. Have sent several out for people to test. Have gotten several very different replies in return. Most think they are a reasonable replacement. I'm still not sure on the final outcome. My latest idea is to modify the speaker steel frame slightly and add a gasket so it is a direct replacement with no mods needed. Stay tuned?!!<P>Rodney Dickman||||reg||1
